<title>BELGIUM: Belgian yr/yr inflation 2.53 pct in Dec.</title>
<headline>Belgian yr/yr inflation 2.53 pct in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Economic Affairs Ministry released the following data on inflation -</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CONSUMER PRICES     Dec	  Nov	  Dec  1995</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1988)	 123.79     123.57     120.74</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.18	 0.15	 0.02</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change (in pct)	   2.53	 2.36	 1.46</p>
<p>NOTE - consensus forecast for Dec CPI was -0.01 percent mo/mo, 2.30 percent yr/yr.</p>
<p>    Health index *		  121.29     121.12</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.14	 0.10</p>
<p>NOTE - * excludes unhealthy products such as tobacco, alcohol and petrol, is used for inflation adjustments of rents and wages.</p>
<p>The ministry said price rises were mainly seen for fresh vegetables and fruit, holiday villages and restaurants and cafes, while for foreign travel lower prices were recorded.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
